course: dictionary
lesson: 6656
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning the writer means. Nursery is a good example. «On Monday he stood on a chair at nursery and bellowed "FINISH HIM!" at a boy holding a toy dinosaur.» Here nursery is a place where small children go, because the boy is very small and is shouting at a classmate.
explain: Now read this: «Mangroves are also a nursery for young fish.» A fish does not go to school, so nursery cannot mean a school here. Ask yourself: what would fit? A safe place where young things grow fits well. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Clues can also tell you about friendship and time. «Sam had been his mate since nursery» means they were friends since they were very small. Nursery can mean a place, a room, or even a time in your life. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A nursery is a place where young children are cared for while parents work, before school.
fact: A nursery can also be a baby's bedroom, or a place where plants and trees are grown and sold.
fact: In the UK, a nursery class is the first class for children aged about three to four.
fact: «Nursery rhyme» means a short, simple song or poem for small children, such as «Ring a ring o' roses».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «On Monday he stood on a chair at nursery and bellowed "FINISH HIM!"» Where was the boy? | In a garden where plants are sold | At the top of the stairs | In a shop that sells toys | *In a place for very young children
exercise: «Mangroves are also a nursery for young fish.» What does nursery mean here? | *A safe place where young things grow | A school for fish | A bedroom | A place where plants are sold
exercise: Ella says, «A plant nursery sells trees.» What does plant nursery mean? | *A place where plants and trees are grown and sold | A short song for small children | A bedroom for a baby | A school for small children
test: «Sam had been his mate since nursery.» When did Sam and the speaker become friends? | *When they were very small | At the big fight | When they were grown up | Last week
test: Which phrase means a short, simple song for small children? | *Nursery rhyme | Plant nursery | Nursery nurse | Nursery school
exam: In «a real old nursery rhyme», what is a nursery rhyme? | A place for babies to sleep | A class for children aged three to four | A place where plants are grown | *A short, simple song for small children
